{% lede %}
Wasteland used satire and T.S. Eliot's poetry to take on spiritual and cultural decline. Part dark physical comedy, part apocalyptic B-movie farce, it follows the last free-thinking clowns as they are hunted by an authoritarian Mime regime, in a world where laughter is resistance. I played Father Strange.
{% /lede %}
